{#
    The sign-in mask — the admin's first real page.

    EVERY VALUE HERE IS ESCAPED BY TWIG, which is the reason this is a template and not a
    concatenated string: `alias` comes straight back from what somebody typed, and `error` is
    assembled from a core response. One forgotten `htmlspecialchars()` in a string version
    would be an injection point that looks like working markup.

    THE DOCUMENT AROUND IT COMES FROM `layout.html.twig` — doctype, head, stylesheet, import map
    and the Turbo import all live there since 002-002-0001. Turbo is what makes the form below
    submit without a full page load; it is not wired up here because it is wired up for every
    page at once.

    NO NAVIGATION, ON PURPOSE: the layout's `nav` block stays unfilled. Whoever sees this page is
    not signed in, and a menu of things they cannot open would be the wrong offer.

    NO STIMULUS, for the same reason as before: the mask has no interactive widget, so it
    declares no `controllers` and the layout leaves the library unloaded. Loading it to do
    nothing is still loading it.
#}{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block bodyAttributes %} class="login-page"{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<main class="login">
    <h1 class="login__title">{{ title }}</h1>

    {% if error %}
        <p class="login__error" role="alert">{{ error }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    <form class="login__form" method="post" action="{{ action }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ tokenField }}" value="{{ token }}">

        <label class="login__label" for="login-alias">Benutzername</label>
        <input class="login__input"
               id="login-alias"
               type="text"
               name="alias"
               value="{{ alias }}"
               autocomplete="username"
               autocapitalize="none"
               required
               autofocus>

        <label class="login__label" for="login-pass">Passwort</label>
        <input class="login__input"
               id="login-pass"
               type="password"
               name="pass"
               autocomplete="current-password"
               required>

        <button class="login__submit" type="submit">Anmelden</button>
    </form>
</main>
{% endblock %}
